<!-- Draft text. Every sentence here should be rewritten in Roy's own words. -->
<div class="eyebrow">About</div>
<h1>An inventory, not a prophecy</h1>
<p class="standfirst">I have spent a long time inside operating systems, compilers, security and servers. This is where I think aloud about what software becomes next.</p>

<section class="split" aria-labelledby="h-who">
<h2 id="h-who">Who is writing</h2>
<div>
<p>My name is Roy. [TWO OR THREE LINES ON YOUR WORK, IN YOUR OWN WORDS: what you built, what you maintain.]</p>
<p>I mention it only so that you know where these opinions come from.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="split" aria-labelledby="h-method" style="display:block">
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 40px">
<h2 id="h-method" style="flex:0 0 160px;margin:0;font-family:var(--text);font-size:12px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass)">The method</h2>
<p style="flex:1 1 420px;margin:0;max-width:620px">I do not start from the announcements. I start from the record.</p>
</div>
<ol class="roman steps" style="margin-top:28px;border-top-color:var(--rule)">
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">I</div><div class="txt"><p>Go back through the history of computing and pick out what was worth building.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">II</div><div class="txt"><p>Ask of each piece, without hurry, whether the age of AI still needs it.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">III</div><div class="txt"><p>Keep what survives, in computer science, in industry and in the market, and see what it adds up to. That may be the software of the next era.</p></div></li>
</ol>
</section>

<section class="split" aria-labelledby="h-not" style="border-top:0;padding-top:0">
<h2 id="h-not">What you will not find</h2>
<div>
<p>Quick verdicts. To say that software is finished, or that this or that no longer matters, takes one sentence and teaches nothing. The sorting is where the judgement is, and it is slow.</p>
<p>I would rather do it in public and be questioned.</p>
<p class="btn-row small" style="margin-top:28px;font-weight:600"><a href="/archive">Start reading</a> <a href="/principles">Read the principles</a></p>
</div>
</section>
</main>
